{#
   One token of a target list — a transition's `target`, a state's initial
   transition, a `<history>`'s default — as the Rust policy spells it.

   A `<history>` is not a state and has no State variant: it is named in the
   machine's History enum, and the engine's entry procedures dereference it
   to what it recorded or to its default. Every other token is a State. The
   Rust twin of `cpp_entry_target.jinja2`.

   `history_states` and `machine_name` are passed in rather than read from the
   caller's context because an imported macro does not see it.
#}
{% macro entry_target(token, history_states, machine_name) -%}
{%- if token in history_states -%}::sce_rust_runtime::EntryTarget::History({{ machine_name }}History::{{ token | to_state_variant }})
{%- else -%}::sce_rust_runtime::EntryTarget::State({{ machine_name }}State::{{ token | to_state_variant }})
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}

{# A whole target list, as a `&'static` slice the policy hands the engine. #}
{% macro entry_targets(tokens, history_states, machine_name) -%}
&[{% for t in tokens %}{{ entry_target(t, history_states, machine_name) }}{{ ", " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}]
{%- endmacro %}
